  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene13_FAQ_2
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: For metal wires at a steady temperature, yes, and that covers most of what
    you meet in a school lab. Some things, like bulb filaments that heat up, or diodes,
    do not keep a constant resistance, so their V-I graph is not a straight line.
    Scientists call the well-behaved ones ohmic conductors.
  ttsText: For metal wires at a steady temperature, yes, and that covers most of
    what you meet in a school lab. Some things, like bulb filaments that heat up,
    or diodes, do not keep a constant resistance, so their V-I graph is not a straight
    line. Scientists call the well-behaved ones ohmic conductors.
